See AGENTS.md and docs/ for full project guidance.

TL;DR:
- Next.js 16 (App Router, React 19) + Drizzle + Neon Postgres on Vercel.
- TDD is the default. Write a failing test in tests/ first, then implement.
  Never commit with red tests. Precommit hook enforces it.
- README.md is a non-technical visitor showcase. Stack, scripts, "Shipped" and
  the technical roadmap live in docs/DEVELOPMENT.md; update it in the SAME
  commit. Visitor-visible changes also update the README showcase.
- Don't reintroduce Supabase.
- No "what" comments — only "why", when non-obvious.
- Tests live in tests/, never co-located. Run with `npm test`.
- Verify with: npm run lint && npm run type-check && npm test && npm run build
- User-facing copy is Russian and follows docs/08-product-voice.md: cool,
  sharp, compact, informal. Code/docs are English.
- DB/class/relation diagrams live in docs/10-data-model.md; keep them in sync
  with lib/schema.ts and route contracts.
